Ted mistakenly wrote <math>2^m\cdot\sqrt{\frac{1}{4096}}</math> as <math>2\cdot\sqrt[m]{\frac{1}{4096}}.</math> What is the sum of all real numbers <math>m</math> for which these two expressions have the same value?

